# WinExec arg0 is a whole command line, so a non-literal there is injection (line 11).
# Line 12 -- ShellExecute(0, 'open', PChar(Cmd), nil, nil, ...) -- is SILENT since the
# owner ruling of 2026-08-27: with nil lpParameters and a plain literal verb there is no
# command line, so CWE-78 cannot occur. See run_shellexec_fixed_scheme.ps1 for what that
# gives up, and run_shellexec_precision.ps1 for what still fires.
unsafe-shellexecute 11
!unsafe-shellexecute 12
!unsafe-shellexecute 17
!unsafe-shellexecute 18
